      "id": "raswyi2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Importance of Agriculture in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Indian agriculture is structured around three major cropping seasons: Kharif, Rabi, and Zaid.",
        "Crops are broadly categorized into major food crops (like rice and wheat) and cash crops (like cotton and sugarcane).",
        "Various farming methods are practiced across the country, ranging from subsistence farming to commercial agriculture.",
        "The Green Revolution played a pivotal role in modernizing crop production and achieving food security in India.",
        "Irrigation development and government initiatives continue to address ongoing structural challenges in Indian agriculture."
      ],
      "id": "jr3ru24"
    },
